# Row B12: consumer construction (x/apibench/b12). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./x/apibench/b12
BENCH=BenchmarkAPI/Construct
REF=struct
AUTO_KEY=b12
# the benchmark configuration: this row is one of the MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE API shapes.
# Only one shape can be the API, so a shape the API did not take is a loser
# in §9.4(5)'s sense and cannot be retained as a profile the way a §9.1 arm
# can.
CLASS=B
#
# `git worktree add <path> d802b9e4e8c9` restores every shape this row
# measured, which is what makes a re-ratification on a pinned host still
# possible.
REMOVED=retired
ADR=6
TITLE="Consumer construction: config struct or positional signature with options (B12)"
# Construction happens once per consumer, so BenchmarkAPI/Construct is not the
# reason either shape would be chosen; it exists so that a construction that
# turned out to be expensive per call is visible rather than assumed away.
#
# §9.2's evidence is "DX review; option growth", and it is three things. The
# line counts (TestTasks): the positional form is 1/1/2 lines for the minimal,
# typical and full constructions against the struct form's 3/4/6, which is the
# clearest DX difference any row in this slice produced. The misuse table: a
# required parameter that is a parameter cannot be omitted (compile error)
# while a required struct field can (run-time refusal) — and NEITHER shape can
# catch the exchange of the topic and the subscription, because both are
# strings; that is the row's finding and the reason §9.2 keeps the struct as
# the primary form with positional sugar. A stray zero-valued option is a
# fifth case: the positional form refuses it at run time, and the struct form
# has no option token for a caller to leave empty. And option growth (TestOptionGrowth):
# a new optional parameter is free for both, while a new required one is a
# field for the struct form and an arity change — every caller — for the other.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="struct with optional positional sugar in 'mq.Quick*' helpers (DX review; option growth)"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: x/apibench/b12 has no IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX
# branch, and its three rows per kind are the construction at zero, one and
# three options, which is the option growth §9.2 asks about.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="opts=0 opts=1 opts=3"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op"
# "DX review" is the other half of §9.2's evidence and is not a metric; the
# construction line counts are in x/apibench/scoring's scorecard.json.
